<title>GERMANY: Buba says German H1 GDP rose 0.7 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Buba says German H1 GDP rose 0.7 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bundesbank gave the following details of H1 1996 GDP data:</p>
<p>PAN-GERMAN GDP	 H1 96	H2 95	  H1 95</p>
<p> hlf/hlf (pct)	  +0.3	 +0.5(+0.4)   +1.1</p>
<p> yr/yr (pct)	    +0.7	 +1.5	   +2.6</p>
<p> GDP (bln dm)	1,519.9    1,516(1,515.3) 1,509.1</p>
<p>WEST GERMAN GDP</p>
<p> hlf/hlf (pct)	  +0.4	 +0.3		 +0.9</p>
<p> yr/yr (pct)	    +0.7	 +1.3(+1.2)	 +2.2(+2.3)</p>
<p> GDP (bln dm)	1,380.1    1,375.1(1,377.9) 1,370.3(1,374.1)</p>
<p>EAST GERMAN GDP</p>
<p> hlf/hlf (pct)	  -0.7	 +1.5(+1.6)	+2.6(+3.0)</p>
<p> yr/yr (pct)	    +0.8	 +4.0(+4.5)	+6.2(+6.1)</p>
<p> GDP (bln dm)	  139.9	140.9(137.3)    138.8(135.1)</p>
<p>NOTE - The changes are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank GDP data. The figures are seasonally adjusted.</p>
<p>Previously announced data in brackets.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
</text>
